=begin pod

=TITLE App::GitManager

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    gitmanager status
    gitmanager status --all --repo=/path/to/parent
    gitmanager status --json
    gitmanager sync --repo=/path/to/repo --dry-run
    gitmanager sync --repo=/path/to/repo
    gitmanager sync --repo=/path/to/repo --yes
    gitmanager sync --repo=/path/to/repo --push --yes

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<App::GitManager> inspects repositories and cautiously synchronizes one
checked-out branch at a time with its configured upstream remote.

=head1 STATUS

C<status> reads the working tree, branch information, and locally cached
remote-tracking references. With C<--all>, it examines immediate subdirectories
of C<--repo> that contain a C<.git> entry (including linked worktrees).

It does not fetch or contact GitHub. Ahead/behind counts for C<status> are
based on the last locally fetched remote-tracking references.

=head1 SYNC (PHASE 2)

C<sync> is intentionally restricted to a single repository; C<--all> is not
permitted. It requires a clean working tree, an attached branch, and a
configured upstream belonging to the selected remote (default C<origin>).

After confirmation, C<sync> fetches with C<--no-tags>, reevaluates the branch,
and performs C<git merge --ff-only> only when the upstream is ahead and no
local commits diverge. It never silently merges, rebases, resets, deletes
branches, or force-pushes.

Local commits are never pushed by default. C<--push> explicitly opts into a
normal, non-force push to the configured upstream branch. If the remote has
advanced incompatibly, Git rejects the push. Pushing is performed only after
another state check.

C<--dry-run> previews planned operations using cached refs without fetching,
pushing, or modifying the repository. It cannot know remote changes that have
not yet been fetched. C<--dry-run> does not require C<--yes>.

When C<--yes> is omitted, C<sync> prompts interactively. C<--no-interactive>
refuses to prompt and requires C<--yes> for an actual sync. Nonterminal input
also requires C<--yes>.

=head1 OPTIONS

=item C<--repo=PATH>       Repository path (or parent for status --all).
=item C<--all>             Inspect immediate child repositories (status only).
=item C<--remote=NAME>     Selected remote, default C<origin>.
=item C<--json>            Machine-readable report.
=item C<--verbose>         Include branch lists in status.
=item C<--dry-run>         Preview sync without network or mutations.
=item C<--yes>             Authorize safe sync actions without confirmation.
=item C<--no-interactive>  Fail rather than prompt for confirmation.
=item C<--push>            Additionally push local commits (sync only).
=item C<--help>            Show usage information.

=head1 EXIT CODES

0 on success, 1 on a Git error, refusal, or cancellation; 2 on invalid
options or absent noninteractive authorization.

=head1 DEVELOPMENT

Run C<zef test .> for unit tests and C<mi6 test> to include integration tests
in C<xt/>. Integration tests use local temporary Git repositories only.

=head1 ROADMAP

Future phases: C<pr>, C<prune-branches>, and C<release>.

=end pod
